{
	"UUID": "f4a20e6b-8c31-4d97-a5e2-1b7c93f0d485",
	"Name": "Okta Threat Overview",
	"Description": "The detections that matter most, on one page, so you can see whether anything is happening without enabling a single scheduled search.\n\nTop row: Okta's own opinion, via ThreatInsight and behaviour rules. Middle: the credential attack shapes, brute force and password spraying, invalid credential volume by source, and MFA fatigue. Bottom: session anomalies and proxied authentication.\n\nEvery tile is one of the kit's detection queries, so what you see here is exactly what the corresponding scheduled search would alert on. Use it to pick which detections to enable and to sanity-check thresholds before you do.",
